 "_doc": "How a FreeSewing design is built (cloth.py): the parts used as pieces (fold = cut on the fold at x = 0, mirrored whole; copies = the same part cut again), alterations every build applies (turned plackets), where each piece starts round the body (wrap), the seam table (edges 'piece:a>b' or 'piece:a>via>b'; a side may be a chain of edges), point stitches (buttons), interfaced pieces, and the tailoring words mapped onto the design's options (ease as a fraction of the body measurement, lengths in m).",
